    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The goblin mood swings comment was just a little aside, a nod to the unpredictable nature of the Toronto real estate market. You can think of it as a metaphor for the ebbs and flows of the market, like a goblin's emotions can shift from calm to chaotic in an instant.\n\nNow, let's get back to the escrow account. When the closing date arrives, the escrow agent (usually a lawyer or a title company) reviews the transaction to ensure everything is in order. They verify that all conditions have been met, such as the inspection reports, financing, and any other contingencies.\n\nOnce everything checks out, the escrow agent releases the funds from the escrow account to the seller. This is usually done electronically, and the funds are transferred to the seller's account. It's like a magical transfer of funds, where the goblin guardian of the escrow account waves its wand and makes the money disappear into thin air.\n\nAs for who's in charge of the account, the escrow agent is responsible for managing the funds and ensuring that the transaction is completed according to the terms of the agreement. They're like the goblin's trusted advisor, making sure everything runs smoothly and according to plan.\n\nIn Toronto,",
